WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Our vector moves three units right and four units up. We want
the part pointing along the diagonal.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.067
Choose a unit vector along the diagonal. Its length is one, so
a dot product measures distance along it.

3
00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:18.400
The dot product is seven divided by the square root of two,
about four point nine five.

4
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:25.133
Multiply this distance by the unit direction. The projection
ends at three point five, three point five.

5
00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:33.267
The projection misses the original tip. What vector joins
them? Predict its coordinates, then pause before the answer.

6
00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:41.400
Subtract the projection from the original vector. The residual
is minus one half, one half, perpendicular to the diagonal.

7
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:49.867
Projection plus residual rebuilds the original vector. One
part follows the chosen direction; the other is perpendicular.

